            (1, 'Why may cutting sleep to study be "self-defeating"?', 'Because without sleep the brain cannot strengthen learning, so the extra study is less useful.', None),
            (2, 'How do teenagers\' body clocks change?', 'They feel sleepy later at night and want to wake later', ['They wake earlier', 'They need no sleep', 'They sleep only in the day']),
            (2, 'Name two effects of chronic lack of sleep.', 'Poor concentration, irritability and greater risk of accidents (any two).', None),
            (3, 'What does melatonin do?', 'It signals the body to sleep', ['It keeps us awake', 'It improves eyesight', 'It cools the room']),
            (3, 'What do doctors advise about devices?', 'Switch them off at least an hour before bed and keep them out of the bedroom.', None),
            (4, 'Which of these is NOT suggested to reset the body clock?', 'Drinking coffee at night', ['A regular bedtime', 'A dark, cool room', 'A morning walk in daylight']),
            (4, 'What did schools that tried later start times report?', 'Better attendance and results.', None),
            (2, 'Which word in paragraph 3 means "lasting for a long time or recurring"?', 'chronically', ['naturally', 'combined', 'irritability']),
